# wrangler local state (persisted Durable Object storage)
.wrangler/

# `wrangler dev` reads secrets from .dev.vars. The Worker has no secrets any more
# (docs/deployment.md §3.2), so there is nothing to put in one — but the ignore stays,
# because THIS REPO IS PUBLIC and a file created later would otherwise be committed
# by the next `git add -A`.
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*

# The admin centre's real credentials — database password, admin token, admin path.
#
# Written by the deploy from GitHub environment secrets (docs/deployment.md §3.1) and
# written by hand when driving the API locally. It was NEVER ignored, only never yet
# created by anyone running `git add -A`; on a public repo that is a loaded gun rather
# than a convention. `api/config.example.php` is the committed shape.
#
# Two locations: the repo root is where the deploy now puts it — beside `dist/`,
# mirroring "beside `/www`" on the host (docs/deployment.md §3.1). `api/config.php`
# is the older location, kept ignored for anyone still testing against it by hand.
/config.php
api/config.php

# A local copy of dist-private/hosts.json for the same reason — see docs/testing.md
# §1.1a-bis. The real one lives in shared/hosts.json and IS committed; this is only
# ever a copy placed at the repo root to mirror "beside /www" while testing.
/hosts.json
